  "title": "4-bit up counter",
  "tier": "T3",
  "description": "Build a 4-bit ripple counter from toggle (T) flip-flops. The CLK lever is the clock: every time it is switched ON (rising edge) the count (lamps Q3 .. Q0 as a binary number, Q0 = least significant) goes up by one and wraps from 15 to 0. Switching CLK off changes nothing. All lamps are off at the start. A T flip-flop toggles on a rising edge of its input: locked repeaters give a master/slave design. Library hint (component tier only): a T flip-flop and a NOT gate are available.",
